## Code Quality Standards

### Architecture and Design
- **Clean Architecture**: Verify proper separation of concerns between layers (presentation, business, data)
- **SOLID Principles**: Ensure Single Responsibility, Open/Closed, Liskov Substitution, Interface Segregation, and Dependency Inversion
- **Design Patterns**: Identify appropriate use of design patterns and flag anti-patterns
- **Dependency Management**: Review dependency injection usage and avoid circular dependencies
- **Modularity**: Ensure proper package organization and module boundaries

### Code Structure
- **Method Length**: Flag methods exceeding 20 lines (aim for 5-10 lines)
- **Class Size**: Review classes with more than 200 lines
- **Cyclomatic Complexity**: Identify overly complex methods (McCabe complexity > 10)
- **Nesting Depth**: Flag deeply nested code (more than 3 levels)
- **Code Duplication**: Identify and suggest refactoring for duplicated code

## WoS Bot Architecture Best Practices

### Module Organization
- **Module Boundaries**: Verify proper module dependencies (wos-ot has no deps, wos-hmi depends on all)
- **Package Structure**: Review package organization within modules (task.impl, task.helper, emulator.impl)
- **Service Pattern**: Verify singleton pattern usage (getServices(), getInstance() methods)
- **Repository Pattern**: Review repository interfaces and implementations

### Task System
- **Task Registration**: Verify tasks are registered in DelayedTaskRegistry
- **Task Enum**: Check task is added to TpDailyTaskEnum
- **Configuration Keys**: Verify configuration keys added to EnumConfigurationKey
- **Helper Usage**: Review use of existing helpers instead of duplicating code
- **Rescheduling**: Ensure tasks always reschedule (even on failure)
- **Logging**: Verify proper use of ProfileLogger with appropriate log levels

### JavaFX Patterns
- **FXML Controllers**: Review controller initialization, FXML binding, event handlers
- **Service Interaction**: Verify controllers interact with services properly
- **Thread Safety**: Ensure JavaFX operations on JavaFX Application Thread
- **UI Updates**: Review use of Platform.runLater() for background thread updates

## Security Review Guidelines

### Input Validation and Data Protection
- **User Input**: Validate all user inputs in JavaFX forms and configuration
- **SQL Injection**: Hibernate handles parameterized queries, but verify HQL query construction
- **Data Exposure**: Check for sensitive data in logs (Discord tokens, profile data)
- **Configuration Storage**: Review how sensitive configuration is stored (SQLite database)

### Emulator and ADB Security
- **ADB Access**: Verify ADB operations are local-only, no remote access
- **Emulator Paths**: Review emulator executable path validation
- **Process Execution**: Verify safe execution of emulator console commands

## Performance and Scalability

### Database and Hibernate
- **N+1 Query Problem**: Identify and resolve N+1 query issues in HQL queries
- **Lazy Loading**: Review entity relationships and fetch strategies
- **Query Optimization**: Analyze HQL queries for performance, use appropriate joins
- **Connection Pooling**: Verify HikariCP configuration for SQLite
- **Batch Operations**: Review batch saves for configurations

### Caching Strategy
- **Screenshot Caching**: Verify screenshot caching per emulator (lastScreenshotCache)
- **Device Caching**: Review ADB device instance caching with TTL (30s)
- **Status Caching**: Check emulator running status caching (5s TTL)
- **Cache Invalidation**: Verify proper cache invalidation on emulator restart

### OCR and Image Processing
- **OCR Region Precision**: Review OCR region definitions (smaller = better accuracy)
- **Settings Reuse**: Verify reuse of DTOTesseractSettings instances
- **Retry Logic**: Check OCR retry mechanisms (TextRecognitionRetrier)
- **Image Processing**: Review OpenCV usage for efficiency

### Concurrency and Threading
- **Thread Safety**: Review shared resources and synchronization
- **Concurrent Collections**: Verify proper use of concurrent data structures
- **Async Processing**: Review @Async and CompletableFuture usage
- **ThreadLocal Usage**: Ensure proper ThreadLocal cleanup

## Error Handling and Logging

### Exception Management
- **Exception Hierarchy**: Review custom exception classes and inheritance
- **Global Exception Handling**: Verify @ControllerAdvice and @ExceptionHandler usage
- **Resource Cleanup**: Ensure proper resource cleanup in finally blocks or try-with-resources
- **Error Responses**: Review error response structure and information disclosure

### Logging Best Practices
- **Log Levels**: Verify appropriate log level usage (DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR)
- **Structured Logging**: Review log message structure and context
- **Performance Impact**: Assess logging performance impact
- **Security**: Ensure no sensitive information in logs

## Testing Coverage and Quality

### Unit Testing
- **Test Coverage**: Verify minimum 80% code coverage for business logic
- **Test Naming**: Review test method naming conventions
- **Test Structure**: Ensure AAA (Arrange-Act-Assert) pattern
- **Mock Usage**: Review proper mocking with Mockito
- **Test Data**: Verify test data management and cleanup

### Integration Testing
- **@SpringBootTest**: Review Spring Boot test configurations
- **TestContainers**: Verify proper use of TestContainers for database testing
- **API Testing**: Review REST API test implementation
- **Security Testing**: Verify security configuration testing

## Code Style and Conventions

### Naming Conventions
- **Classes**: PascalCase (e.g., UserService, OrderRepository)
- **Methods**: camelCase (e.g., findUserById, processOrder)
- **Variables**: camelCase (e.g., userId, orderTotal)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., MAX_RETRY_COUNT)
- **Packages**: lowercase with dots (e.g., com.company.service)

### Documentation
- **Javadoc**: Ensure public APIs have proper Javadoc
- **Comments**: Review inline comments for clarity and necessity
- **README**: Verify project documentation is up to date
- **API Documentation**: Review OpenAPI/Swagger documentation

## Memory Management and Resource Usage

### Resource Management
- **AutoCloseable**: Verify proper use of try-with-resources
- **Memory Leaks**: Identify potential memory leak sources
- **Resource Pooling**: Review connection and object pooling strategies
- **GC Pressure**: Assess garbage collection impact

### Collection Usage
- **Collection Types**: Verify appropriate collection type selection
- **Initial Capacity**: Review collection initialization with proper capacity
- **Primitive Collections**: Consider primitive collections for performance
- **Memory Efficiency**: Assess memory usage patterns

